{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S2 (f184) CLOSED with both attestations after the completion-verifier fix; unblocked S3 (2932), S4 (dc0d), S5 (343b). Starting S4. NEW DISCIPLINE applied from the S2 close failure: mutation testing verifies the tests you HAVE and cannot find the test you never WROTE — so (a) pre-remediate each plan BEFORE its first review instead of fixing findings serially, and (b) add an AC requiring every criterion to be discharged by a NAMED test, listed on the ticket before close. S4 pre-remediation applied without waiting for a BLOCK: fixed the stale _pai_check_config citation (:653 -> :718 after S1/S2 moved code); RESOLVED the openai-registration ambiguity in the plan text (register the openai builder ONLY when cfg.base_url is set, so a bare openai:gpt-4o keeps S1s lazy-string path and the openai SDK stays optional — this does NOT make base_url a selector, and it matches the documented recipe at docs/llm-framework.md:131-133 which sets REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER=openai explicitly alongside REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL); recorded the providers.py 225/300 LOC budget against S1s ATTESTED cap; added a regression-guard AC for the bare-openai lazy path, a full-make-test AC, and the named-test-per-criterion AC. Verified S4s other citations are accurate: config.py:502-503 and :611-612 correct, docs recipe present at :131-133, test_unsupported_config_is_a_loud_error at test_pydantic_ai_runner.py:255."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785376362887517001,"uuid":"2a77f9a2-bd41-47ff-9e03-eb2a1a08d59b"}